3. STOREFRONT PLACEMENT CHANNELS
==================================================

Partner Picks products may appear in five different
placement channels:

A. STORE BANNER

Partner products may appear within the existing
blue store banner.

They should be integrated with the store's own
products rather than replacing all native products.

B. STORE PRODUCT GRID

Partner products may appear between ordinary
product cards.

They must visually integrate with the existing
product card design.

C. DISCOVER MORE PRODUCTS

Partner products may appear in the existing
Discover More Products section on product landing
pages.

D. REELS FEED

Partner Picks products may appear naturally between
Reels while users browse the Reels feed.

Requirements:

- Never interrupt an actively playing Reel.
- Never force users to watch promotional content.
- Never require waiting before continuing.
- Allow users to skip and continue browsing.
- Use a presentation compatible with the existing
  Reels interface.
- Link directly to the original product landing page.

E. STORIES

Partner Picks products may appear naturally while
users navigate Stories.

Requirements:

- Do not interrupt an actively viewed Story.
- Do not insert promotional Stories after every
  ordinary Story.
- Maintain natural navigation.
- Avoid excessive repetition.
- Provide a direct path to the original product
  landing page.

All five placement channels must be investigated
against the existing project architecture.

Do not assume that Reels and Stories currently use
the same rendering or content delivery mechanism.

