IMPORTANT PRODUCT SHARING SCENARIO:

Merchant A owns three products.

Merchant A wants to share those same three products
with Merchant B and Merchant C.

The system must allow the same three products to
appear in both partner stores independently.

Sharing a product with B must not consume the
product-sharing allowance for C.

The product limit is evaluated independently
within each partnership.

DEFAULT PRODUCT SELECTION:

The default behavior should allow a merchant to
select one common product collection for all partners.

However, merchants must also have the option to
customize product selection separately for each
partnership.

