11. RECIPROCAL EXPOSURE AND FAIRNESS
==================================================

Fair exposure is essential.

Example:

Merchant A has one partner.
Merchant B has five partners.

The fact that B has additional partners must not
automatically reduce A's fair exposure within
the A-B partnership.

Exposure fairness must be evaluated within each
partnership independently.

Study and propose a fair exposure algorithm.

Consider:

- Impressions.
- Unique exposure opportunities.
- Placement type.
- Exposure duration.
- Product rotation.
- Product count.
- Partnership agreement.
- Available inventory.
- User frequency limits.
- Different traffic volumes.

The algorithm should not promise equal impressions
when actual traffic and available opportunities
are different.

Instead, propose a measurable and transparent
fairness model.

Expose relevant statistics to both merchants.

